--TEST--
A local cache entry may be absent at any time: a miss answers `null` rather than throwing, and an unreachable shared store does the opposite — ADR 0059 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $cache = Core\Cache::local();

// § 1: any entry may be absent at any time, for any reason. A miss is an
// ordinary answer, so nothing here is a `try` — a program that would be
// incorrect when this happens is using the wrong tier, and that is the whole
// contract this member offers.
var $missing = $cache->get("nothing-wrote-this") ?? "absent";
echo "missing=", $missing as string, "\n";

// The same member, the same question, one write later: absence is not an error
// state the store enters, it is what a key with no entry answers.
$cache->put("written", "value");
var $written = $cache->get("written") as string;
echo "written=", $written, "\n";

// § 1's other side, and the reason the two tiers cannot be one member: an
// unreachable store *throws*. Absence is an answer here and a failure there, so
// a caller that would be incorrect on a miss has to be able to say which of the
// two it asked for.
try {
    Core\Cache::shared();
    echo "shared answered\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo "shared threw rather than answering absent\n";
}
--EXPECT--
missing=absent
written=value
shared threw rather than answering absent
